            translationEn:
              '(124) Those are the ones who disbelieve in the verses of their Lord and in [their] meeting Him, so their deeds have become worthless; and We will not assign to them on the Day of Resurrection any importance. (125) Say, "If the sea were ink for [writing] the words of my Lord, the sea would be exhausted before the words of my Lord were exhausted." (126) And mention in the Book, Abraham. Indeed, he was a man of truth and a prophet. (127) And mention in the Book, Ishmael. Indeed, he was true to his promise, and he was a messenger and a prophet. And he used to enjoin on his people prayer and zakah. (128) Does man not remember that We created him before, while he was nothing? (129) Go, both of you, to Pharaoh. Indeed, he has transgressed. And speak to him with gentle speech that perhaps he may be reminded or fear [Allah]. (130) [Allah] said, "Fear not. Indeed, I am with you both; I hear and I see." (131) [Pharaoh] said, "So who is the Lord of you two, O Moses?" He said, "Our Lord is He who gave each thing its form and then guided [it]." (132) From the earth We created you, and into it We will return you, and from it We will extract you another time. (133) And indeed, I am the Perpetual Forgiver of whoever repents and believes and does righteousness and then continues in guidance. (134) So be patient over what they say and exalt [Allah] with praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting. (135) We have certainly sent down to you a Book in which is your mention. Then will you not reason? (136) And We did not create the heaven and earth and that between them in play. (137) And We made from water every living thing. Then will they not believe? (138) And it is He who created the night and the day and the sun and the moon; all [heavenly bodies] in an orbit are swimming. (139) They said, "Who has done this to our gods? Indeed, he is of the wrongdoers." They said, "Are you the one who did this to our gods, O Abraham?" (140) They said, "Burn him and support your gods - if you are to act." We [Allah] said, "O fire, be coolness and safety upon Abraham." (141) And We admitted him into Our mercy. Indeed, he was of the righteous. (142) So We responded to him and saved him and his family from the great affliction. And We saved him from the people who denied Our signs. (143) And he called out within the darknesses, "There is no deity except You; exalted are You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers." So We responded to him and saved him from the distress. And thus do We save the believers. (144) Indeed, Allah will admit those who believe and do righteous deeds to gardens beneath which rivers flow. Indeed, Allah does what He intends. (145) Say, "O mankind, I am only to you a clear warner." So those who have believed and done righteous deeds - for them is forgiveness and noble provision. (146) And it is He who gave you life; then He causes you to die and then will [again] give you life. Indeed, mankind is ungrateful. (147) O you who have believed, bow and prostrate and worship your Lord and do good - that you may succeed. (148) And say, "My Lord, forgive and have mercy, and You are the best of the merciful." (149) Indeed,',
