            translationEn:
              'those who like that immorality should be spread among those who have believed will have a painful punishment in this world and the Hereafter. And Allah knows and you do not know. (150) And rely upon the Ever-Living who does not die, and exalt [Allah] with His praise. (151) And rely upon the Exalted in Might, the Merciful, who sees you when you arise. (152) She said, "Indeed kings - when they enter a city, they ruin it and render the honored of its people humbled. And thus do they do." (153) He said, "My Lord, indeed I have wronged myself, so forgive me," and He forgave him. Indeed, He is the Forgiving, the Merciful. (154) Indeed, [O Muhammad], you do not guide whom you like, but Allah guides whom He wills. And He is most knowing of the [rightly] guided. (155) And do not invoke with Allah another deity. There is no deity except Him. Everything will be destroyed except His Face. (156) And We certainly sent Noah to his people, and he remained among them a thousand years minus fifty years, and the flood seized them while they were wrongdoers. But We saved him and the companions of the ship, and We made it a sign for the worlds. (157) And Lot believed him. And [Abraham] said, "Indeed, I will emigrate to [the service of] my Lord. Indeed, He is the Exalted in Might, the Wise." (158) Excellent is the reward of the [righteous] workers, who have been patient and upon their Lord rely. (159) He brings the living out of the dead and brings the dead out of the living and brings to life the earth after its lifelessness. (160) And He sends down from the sky rain and brings to life thereby the earth after its lifelessness. Indeed in that are signs for a people who reason. (161) So observe the effects of the mercy of Allah - how He gives life to the earth after its lifelessness. Indeed, that [same one] will give life to the dead, and He is over all things competent. (162) Indeed, those who abuse Allah and His Messenger - Allah has cursed them in this world and the Hereafter and prepared for them a humiliating punishment. (163) Those who disbelieve will have a severe punishment, and those who believe and do righteous deeds will have forgiveness and a great reward. (164) O mankind, you are those in need of Allah, while Allah is the Free of need, the Praiseworthy. If He wills, He can do away with you and bring forth a new creation. And that is for Allah not difficult. (165) Say, "Indeed I fear, if I should disobey my Lord, the punishment of a tremendous Day." (166) Say, "O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Merciful." (167) Indeed, those who have said, "Our Lord is Allah" and then remained on a right course - the angels will descend upon them, [saying], "Do not fear and do not grieve but receive good tidings of Paradise." (168) And Pharaoh called out among his people; he said, "O my people, does not the kingdom of Egypt belong to me, and these rivers flowing beneath me; then do you not see?" (169) Say, "Allah gives you life, then He causes you to die, then He will assemble you for the Day of Resurrection, about which there is no doubt, but most of the people do not know." (170) As for those who believed and did righteous deeds, their Lord will admit them into His mercy. (171) O our people, respond to the Caller of Allah and believe in him; He will forgive for you your sins and protect you from a painful punishment. (172) O you who have believed, if you support Allah, He will support you and plant firmly your feet. (173) O you who have believed, obey Allah and obey the Messenger and do not invalidate your deeds. (174) Indeed, those who pledge allegiance to you, [O Muhammad] - they are actually pledging allegiance to Allah. The hand of Allah is over their hands. (175) Certainly was Allah pleased with the believers when they pledged allegiance to you under the tree, and He knew what was in their hearts, so He sent down tranquility upon them. (176) O you who have believed, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet. (177) Then do they not look at the sky above them - how We structured it and adorned it. (178) But remind by the Quran whoever fears My threat. (179) Indeed, the righteous will be in gardens and springs. (180) And from their properties was [given] the right of the [needy] petitioner and the deprived. (181) Indeed, the punishment of your Lord will occur. Of it there is no preventer. (182) The Most Merciful Taught the Quran, Created man, [And] taught him eloquence. (183) This is Hell, which the criminals deny. (184) And have you seen the water that you drink? Is it you who brought it down from the clouds, or is it We who bring it down? (185) And We are closer to him than you, but you do not see. (186) And why do you not believe in Allah while the Messenger invites you to believe in your Lord and He has taken your covenant, if you should [truly] be believers? (187) Know that Allah gives life to the earth after its lifelessness. We have made clear to you the signs; perhaps you will understand. (188) Allah is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him. Those are the party of Allah. Unquestionably, the party of Allah - they are the successful. (189) And be not like those who forgot Allah, so He made them forget themselves. Those are the defiantly disobedient. Not equal are the companions of the Fire and the companions of Paradise. The companions of Paradise - they are the attainers [of success]. (190) O you who have believed, when the believing women come to you as emigrants, examine them. Allah is most knowing as to their faith. And if you know them to be believers, then do not return them to the disbelievers. (191) Your wealth and your children are but a trial, and Allah has with Him a great reward. (192) She said, "My Lord, build for me near You a house in Paradise and save me from Pharaoh and his deeds and save me from the wrongdoing people." (193) Indeed, those who fear their Lord unseen will have forgiveness and a great reward. (194) Indeed, We sent Noah to his people, [saying], "Warn your people before there comes to them a painful punishment." (195) He said, "My Lord, indeed I invited my people [to truth] night and day. But my invitation increased them not except in flight. And indeed, every time I invited them that You may forgive them, they put their fingers in their ears." (196) And they give food in spite of love for it to the needy, the orphan, and the captive. [Saying], "We feed you only for the countenance of Allah. We wish not from you reward or gratitude." (197) Indeed, the righteous will be in pleasure, and indeed, the wicked will be in Hellfire. (198) And your Lord is going to give you, and you will be satisfied. (199) When the victory of Allah has come and the conquest, And you see the people entering into the religion of Allah in multitudes, Then exalt [Him] with praise of your Lord and ask forgiveness of Him. Indeed, He is ever Accepting of repentance.',
